    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7e2dac38-6c75-5b90-a3c8-58a0d8294e61",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3}$ on $A?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the first and third rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
